 "questions": [
  {
   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "PS9_001_Tic Tac Toe Winner",
   "display_name": "Tic Tac Toe Winner",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>In <b>tic-tac-toe</b>, two players take turns writing <code>X</code> and <code>O</code> on a 3 by 3 board. A player <b>wins</b> if they have three of their marks in a line: a whole <b>row</b>, a whole <b>column</b>, or one of the two <b>diagonals</b>.</p>\n<p>We store the board as a list of 3 rows, where each row is a list of 3 strings: <code>\"X\"</code>, <code>\"O\"</code>, or <code>\".\"</code> for an empty square. For example:</p>\n<pre>board = [[&quot;X&quot;, &quot;O&quot;, &quot;X&quot;],\n         [&quot;O&quot;, &quot;X&quot;, &quot;O&quot;],\n         [&quot;O&quot;, &quot;.&quot;, &quot;X&quot;]]</pre>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#c9e7cf\">X</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">O</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">X</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">O</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#c9e7cf\">X</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">O</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">O</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\"></td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#c9e7cf\">X</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">X has the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right, so X wins</div>\n<p>Here <code>board[r][c]</code> is the square in row <code>r</code> and column <code>c</code>, and the two diagonals are <code>board[0][0], board[1][1], board[2][2]</code> and <code>board[0][2], board[1][1], board[2][0]</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>winner(board)</code> that <b>returns</b> <code>\"X\"</code> if X has three in a line, <code>\"O\"</code> if O has three in a line, and <code>\"Nobody\"</code> if neither has. Three empty squares <code>\".\"</code> in a line do <b>not</b> count as a win. You may assume that at most one player has a line.</p>\n<p><b>Hint:</b> write down the 8 possible lines (3 rows, 3 columns, 2 diagonals) and check each of them: are the three squares equal, and not <code>\".\"</code>?</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>winner([[\"X\", \"O\", \"X\"], [\"O\", \"X\", \"O\"], [\"O\", \".\", \"X\"]])</code> returns <code>\"X\"</code> (the diagonal)</li><li><code>winner([[\"O\", \"O\", \"O\"], [\"X\", \"X\", \".\"], [\".\", \".\", \"X\"]])</code> returns <code>\"O\"</code> (the top row)</li><li><code>winner([[\"X\", \"O\", \"X\"], [\"X\", \"O\", \"O\"], [\"O\", \"X\", \"X\"]])</code> returns <code>\"Nobody\"</code></li></ul>",
   "answerpreload": "def winner(board):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(winner([[\"X\", \"O\", \"X\"], [\"O\", \"X\", \"O\"], [\"O\", \".\", \"X\"]]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
