  {
   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "PS9_002_Run Length Encoding",
   "display_name": "Run Length Encoding",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Long strings with many repeated letters can be stored in a shorter way: instead of writing every letter, we write each <b>run</b> of equal letters once, together with how many times it repeats. This is called <b>run-length encoding</b>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>\"aaabccdddd\"</code> has the runs <code>aaa</code>, <code>b</code>, <code>cc</code> and <code>dddd</code>:</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">s =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(36,103,161);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(41,110,169);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(55,133,192);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(60,140,200);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">6</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">7</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">8</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">9</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">runs: aaa (3), b (1), cc (2), dddd (4)</div>\n<p>so its encoding is the list of tuples</p>\n<pre>[(&quot;a&quot;, 3), (&quot;b&quot;, 1), (&quot;c&quot;, 2), (&quot;d&quot;, 4)]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>encode(s)</code> that takes a string <code>s</code> and <b>returns</b> its run-length encoding: a list of <code>(letter, count)</code> tuples, one for each run, in order. Upper-case and lower-case letters are different (<code>\"A\"</code> and <code>\"a\"</code> are not the same), and spaces and digits are characters like any other. An empty string gives an empty list.</p>\n<p><b>Hint:</b> go through the string one character at a time, keeping track of the <b>current</b> character and how many times you have seen it in a row. When a different character arrives, the current run has ended: save it as a tuple and start a new run. Do not forget to save the very last run after the loop!</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>encode(\"aaabccdddd\")</code> returns <code>[('a', 3), ('b', 1), ('c', 2), ('d', 4)]</code></li><li><code>encode(\"abc\")</code> returns <code>[('a', 1), ('b', 1), ('c', 1)]</code></li><li><code>encode(\"zzzz\")</code> returns <code>[('z', 4)]</code></li><li><code>encode(\"\")</code> returns <code>[]</code></li></ul>",
   "answerpreload": "def encode(s):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(encode(\"aaabccdddd\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"aaabccdddd\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[('a', 3), ('b', 1), ('c', 2), ('d', 4)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"abc\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[('a', 1), ('b', 1), ('c', 1)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"zzzz\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[('z', 4)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"a\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[('a', 1)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"aabbaa\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[('a', 2), ('b', 2), ('a', 2)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"AaaA\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[('A', 1), ('a', 2), ('A', 1)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"  11 \"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[(' ', 2), ('1', 2), (' ', 1)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(encode(\"abbbbbbbbbbbbc\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[('a', 1), ('b', 12), ('c', 1)]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "PS9_003_Merge Booking Slots",
   "display_name": "Merge Booking Slots",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A meeting room is booked for several <b>slots</b> during the day. Each slot is a tuple <code>(start, end)</code> of whole hours, for example <code>(9, 11)</code> means from 9 o'clock to 11 o'clock. Some slots <b>overlap</b>, and the manager wants to know the times when the room is actually busy, as a short list of slots that do not overlap.</p>\n<p>Two slots must be <b>merged</b> into one if they overlap or <b>touch</b> (one ends exactly when the other starts, like <code>(9, 11)</code> and <code>(11, 12)</code>). For example, for the slots <code>[(9, 11), (13, 15), (10, 12), (16, 17)]</code>:</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td></td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">8</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">9</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">10</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">11</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">12</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">13</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">14</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">15</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">16</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">17</td><td style=\"width:26px;font-size:11px;color:#8a939c;text-align:left\">18</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;padding-right:8px;white-space:nowrap\">(9, 11)</td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#4a90c8;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#4a90c8;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;padding-right:8px;white-space:nowrap\">(13, 15)</td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#4a90c8;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#4a90c8;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;padding-right:8px;white-space:nowrap\">(10, 12)</td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#4a90c8;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#4a90c8;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;padding-right:8px;white-space:nowrap\">(16, 17)</td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#4a90c8;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"height:8px\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;padding-right:8px;white-space:nowrap\">merged (9, 12)</td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#2e7a48;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#2e7a48;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#2e7a48;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;padding-right:8px;white-space:nowrap\">merged (13, 15)</td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#2e7a48;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#2e7a48;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:13px;padding-right:8px;white-space:nowrap\">merged (16, 17)</td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:#2e7a48;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td><td style=\"width:26px;height:16px;background:transparent;border-left:1px solid #d3d9df\"></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">blue: the slots as given; green: after merging</div>\n<p><code>(9, 11)</code> and <code>(10, 12)</code> overlap, so they become one slot <code>(9, 12)</code>; the others stay as they are. The answer is <code>[(9, 12), (13, 15), (16, 17)]</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>merge(slots)</code> that takes a list of <code>(start, end)</code> tuples (in any order; in each slot <code>start &lt; end</code>) and <b>returns</b> the list of merged slots, sorted by start time.</p>\n<p><b>Hint:</b> first sort the slots with <code>sorted(slots)</code> (tuples are sorted by their first item, then the second). Then go through them in order, keeping the <b>current</b> merged slot <code>(start, end)</code>: if the next slot starts at or before the current <code>end</code>, it joins the current slot (and the end becomes the later of the two ends); otherwise the current slot is finished, and the next slot becomes the current one.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>merge([(9, 11), (13, 15), (10, 12), (16, 17)])</code> returns <code>[(9, 12), (13, 15), (16, 17)]</code></li><li><code>merge([(9, 11), (11, 12)])</code> returns <code>[(9, 12)]</code> (they touch)</li><li><code>merge([(8, 18), (10, 11)])</code> returns <code>[(8, 18)]</code> (the second slot is inside the first one)</li><li><code>merge([])</code> returns <code>[]</code></li></ul>",
