  {
   "xml_index": 4,
   "xml_name": "PS9_004_Magic Square",
   "display_name": "Magic Square",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A <b>magic square</b> is a square table of numbers where <b>every row</b>, <b>every column</b>, and <b>both diagonals</b> add up to the <b>same</b> total. Here is a famous one, where every line adds up to 15:</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#c9e7cf\">2</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">7</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">9</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#c9e7cf\">5</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">4</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#eef3fa\">3</td><td style=\"width:34px;height:34px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:monospace;font-size:17px;border:2px solid #2b4c7e;background:#c9e7cf\">8</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">rows: 2+7+6, 9+5+1, 4+3+8; columns: 2+9+4, 7+5+3, 6+1+8; diagonals: 2+5+8 (green), 6+5+4: all are 15</div>\n<p>We store the square as a list of rows, where each row is a list of integers:</p>\n<pre>square = [[2, 7, 6],\n          [9, 5, 1],\n          [4, 3, 8]]</pre>\n<p>Here <code>square[r][c]</code> is the number in row <code>r</code> and column <code>c</code>. The square has <code>n</code> rows and <code>n</code> columns, where <code>n = len(square)</code> can be any size from 1 upwards. The two diagonals are the numbers <code>square[i][i]</code> (top-left to bottom-right) and <code>square[i][n - 1 - i]</code> (top-right to bottom-left), for <code>i</code> from <code>0</code> to <code>n - 1</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>is_magic(square)</code> that <b>returns</b> <code>True</code> if all <code>n</code> rows, all <code>n</code> columns and both diagonals have the same sum, and <code>False</code> otherwise. (In this question the numbers may repeat; only the sums matter.)</p>\n<p><b>Hint:</b> compute the sum of the first row, then check that every other line has that same sum.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>is_magic([[2, 7, 6], [9, 5, 1], [4, 3, 8]])</code> returns <code>True</code></li><li><code>is_magic([[1, 2], [2, 1]])</code> returns <code>False</code> (the rows and columns add up to 3, but the diagonals give 2 and 4)</li><li><code>is_magic([[5]])</code> returns <code>True</code></li></ul>",
   "answerpreload": "def is_magic(square):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(is_magic([[2, 7, 6], [9, 5, 1], [4, 3, 8]]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(is_magic([[2, 7, 6], [9, 5, 1], [4, 3, 8]]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(is_magic([[1, 2], [2, 1]]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "False",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
